$\begin{aligned}
& \frac{d x}{d y}+\int y \cdot d x=x^3 \Rightarrow \int y \cdot d x=x^3-\frac{d x}{d y} \\
& \Rightarrow 1+\frac{d y}{d x}\left(\int y \cdot d x\right)=x^3 \cdot \frac{d y}{d x}
\end{aligned}$
Differentiate both sides w.e.t. $x\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow 0+\frac{d y}{d x}(y)+\left(\int y \cdot d x\right)\left(\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}\right)=x^3 \cdot \frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}+\frac{d y}{d x}\left(2 x^2\right) \\
& \Rightarrow y \cdot \frac{d y}{d x}+\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}\left[x^3-\frac{d x}{d y}\right]=x^3 \cdot \frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}+2 x^2 \frac{d y}{d x} \\
& \Rightarrow y \frac{d y}{d x}+x^3 \frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}-\left(\frac{d x}{d y}\right)\left(\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}\right)=x^3 \frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}+2 x^2 \frac{d y}{d x} \\
& \Rightarrow y \frac{d y}{d x}-\frac{d x}{d y} \cdot \frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}=2 x^2 \cdot \frac{d y}{d x}
\end{aligned}$
Multiplying both side by $\frac{d y}{d x}\begin{aligned}
& y\left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)^2-\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}=2 x^2\left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)^2 \\
& \Rightarrow \frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}+\left(2 x^2-y\right)\left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)^2=0 \\
& \text { Order }=2, \text { degree }=1
\end{aligned}$

